{
  "rationale": "Use a small plant split into sensing and motion capability, then layer deterministic specifications that map sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one recovery or exploration action. The policy favors move_forward in clear space, allows occasional random_walk only from clear/search-like conditions, uses brief directed turns for side obstacles, uses a rare one-step move_backward only after front blockage, and reserves full_rotate for a dedicated repeated-failure last-resort path. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not preempted, while obstacle events can still force safe recovery.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability in plant automata.",
    "Use one specification automaton as the main supervisor policy with one-shot action states and total uncontrollable transitions.",
    "Bias strongly toward forward progress: clear -> move_forward by default, with random_walk only as a secondary exploration option after successful forward pulses.",
    "Handle obstacle_left with rotate_clockwise and obstacle_right with rotate_counterclockwise consistently.",
    "Handle obstacle_front through a dedicated backward escape, then short directed turns, and only after repeated blocked outcomes allow a dedicated full_rotate last resort."
  ],
